================================================================================
Background removal (rembg / BiRefNet / U^2-Net / IS-Net)
================================================================================
Background removal is provided by rembg (MIT) and the ONNX models it downloads
(BiRefNet, IS-Net, U^2-Net, Silueta), each under their respective licenses.
  https://github.com/danielgatis/rembg

With the PyTorch engine (the Windows "rocm" install), the BiRefNet models run
natively instead, from the same checkpoints rembg's ONNX files were exported
from:
  - BiRefNet model code, vendored in src/bgbg/birefnet/ (inference only)
    Copyright (c) 2024 ZhengPeng. Licensed under the MIT License
    (src/bgbg/birefnet/LICENSE).
    https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet (revision d8c386b)
  - Its Swin Transformer backbone
    Copyright (c) 2021 Microsoft. Licensed under the MIT License.
    https://github.com/microsoft/Swin-Transformer
  - Weights: BiRefNet's v1 release checkpoints, downloaded on first use.
    https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet/releases/tag/v1

================================================================================
HEIC / HEIF images (pi-heif, libheif, libde265)
================================================================================
The worker reads HEIC/HEIF photos with pi-heif, the decode-only build of
pillow-heif. The installers install it, and the release builds bundle it. Its
binary wheels include libheif and libde265.

  - pi-heif
    Copyright (c) 2021-2023, Pillow-Heif contributors.
    Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
    https://github.com/bigcat88/pillow_heif

  - libheif
    Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0.
    https://github.com/strukturag/libheif

  - libde265
    Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0.
    https://github.com/strukturag/libde265

HEVC decoding may be subject to patents in some countries.

